songs.originalText:
{title:Doxology}
{key:E}

Verse 1:
Praise [E]God from whom all blessings flow;
Praise [E]him all creatures [A]here be[B]low;
Praise [C#m]him a[B]bove, ye h[A]eav’n[B]ly [C#m]host;
Praise [E]Father, [B]Son, and [A]Ho[B]ly [E]Ghost

{title: How great is our God}
{subtitle:Chris Tomlin}
{key:E}
{tempo:76}

VERSE 1:
The [E]splendour of the King, [C#m7]clothed in majesty;
let all the earth rejoice[A], all the earth rejoice.
He wraps[E] himself in light and [C#m7]darkness tries to hide,
and trembles at his voice[A], and trembles at his voice.

CHORUS:
How [E]great is our God, (sing with me)
how [C#m7]great is our God and all will see
how [A]great, how great[B] is our God[E]

VERSE 2:
And [E]age to age he stands, and [C#m7]time is in his hands;
beginning and the end[A2], beginning and the end.
The God[E]head, Three in One, [C#m7]Father, Spirit, Son,
the Lion and the Lamb[A2], the Lion and the Lamb.

BRIDGE:
[E]Name above all names, [C#m7]worthy of all praise;
my [A]heart will sing is our God[E]!
